DESIGN.md:956:| 2026-06-12 | 0.3 | **Spec-gap close** (#195; external design review, triaged in `sessions/phase-5-design-system/external-design-review-2026-06-12.md`). Codifies what the shipped R2 surfaces already render — no new product surfaces (R2.4-compatible); the one forward spec is §7.6's record voice, gating the unshipped Library REVERSE PRD views. Adds: §7.7 controls (primary/secondary/quiet/links/disabled/signal-active/validation) · §7.8 accessibility (focus ring, keyboard, contrast floors, color-never-alone) · §7.9 breakpoints · §7.10 iconography (no icon libraries) · §8.2 verdict→token mapping + chip anatomy (register + panel registers) · §8.8 registers and tables · §7.6 PRD-document "record voice" typography. Promotes the R2.14 Codex catch into law: `warn` is accent-only, never text (§4.3 token-role table). Resolves inconsistencies: unit law `px` never `pt`, `0.75px` intentional (§7.2 rewrite; §4.2) · sanctioned off-scale type ranges 84–96 reading numeral / 64–96 marketing display (§5.2) · marketing spacing extension 96·112 (§6) · lime budget restated as countable (§4.1) · scoped duo constants `DUO_SID`/`DUO_AVIRA` in `lib/design.ts` (§4.4) · dark-mode half-spec cut to one line (§4.5) · favicon brand-mode exception acknowledged (§4.4). |
DESIGN.md:964:| 2026-06-26 | 0.4 | **Dual-color everywhere** (founder-signed; ticket #35, this PR). The dual-color aperture mark becomes the **standard mark on every surface — in-product nav and dashboard included** — replacing the prior "monotone in-product / dual-color brand-surfaces-only / never resting in the nav or dashboard" policy. §1.3 consolidated to two color states (static dual-color default + transient animation); §3 primary horizontal lockup repointed to the duo assets; §4.4 forbidden-`avira` list scoped to *standalone* accents only (the resting duo mark is exempt); §1.5/§11 asset roles updated (duo = standard, mono = fallback). The §9.2 aperture-close animation note is unchanged and still valid. RATIONALE: the founder chose visual brand consistency over the brand-vs-product split — one mark, one color story, on every surface. Code lockstep: `TopNav.tsx` (`SidiraLockup`→`SidiraLockupDuo`) and `AppShellV2.tsx` rail (`ConsoleMarkMono`→`SheetMarkDuo`) now render dual-color in-product. |
